# L §4.4: "A comparison is decided when the whole interval lies on one side. Otherwise it is a hole: ?"date within …
# not precise enough for <the comparison>" (HOLE-IMPRECISE)."  "A value compared with itself is decided ... x < x is
# false and x == x and x <= x are true even when x is a window."  An imprecise date prints as its window (L §5.18).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input d: date

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = window(2020-07-01, 2020-07-31)

ask q1: d, d < 2020-08-01, d > 2020-07-31, d < d, d == d, d <= d
ask q2: d < 2020-07-15
=== expect
q1: (window(2020-07-01, 2020-07-31), true, false, false, true, true)
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: ?"date within window(2020-07-01, 2020-07-31) not precise enough for d < 2020-07-15" (d)
  cut 2026-12-31
